menu "EROS log"

    config EROS_LOG_PANIC_CAPTURE
        bool "Capture panic output into the RTC boot buffer"
        depends on BOOTLOADER_CUSTOM_RESERVE_RTC
        default y
        help
            Wraps the panic handler's print functions (ld --wrap) so a copy
            of the Guru Meditation dump — headline, registers, backtrace —
            lands in the same RTC region as the boot log and is replayed to
            the EROS log group on the next boot. The native UART panic
            output is untouched. Costs a few hundred bytes of IRAM for the
            wrappers.

            The region is CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_CUSTOM_RESERVE_RTC_SIZE bytes;
            a full dump plus the next boot's log can exceed it, in which
            case the tail is dropped (counted, reported at replay).

endmenu
